WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.167
The first number was 1.94 seconds. Flattering, and wrong.

00:00:05.517 --> 00:00:09.433
This was apache/answer moving
from Create React App to Vite.

00:00:09.783 --> 00:00:16.600
The type check had been silently dropped.
Restored, the cold build takes 4.77 seconds.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:22.333
Still a 76 percent improvement over 19.87 seconds.

00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:27.700
The bundle looked smaller too,
partly because two icon fonts never shipped.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.133
Three more failures hid behind a green build.

00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:38.000
One: the server could not find its own assets,
so every page went out without scripts or styles.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:46.067
Two: a blank page with a perfect console. Translations
registered too early, and the app never mounted.

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:52.933
Three: the warning nobody reads.
Exit code zero, and every lazy page would 404.

00:00:53.283 --> 00:01:00.900
Comparing build outputs caught it:
297 JavaScript files had become 114.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:08.667
Coding agents did the mechanical work. Every check had
to fail, on purpose, before it was trusted. Red first.

00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:11.692
A green build is not a working app.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:19.833
Red First starts with a $2,500 audit that maps where
your frontend could pass the build and still break.
